{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 160, :comments ["<b>Head</b> — The beginning of the word: \"Your every command that You have commanded me is truth.\" And Rabbi Yeshuah said: It alludes to the word אנכי (I) at Mount Sinai."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The quotation marks render the implied content Ibn Ezra supplies for 'the beginning of the word'; the Hebrew is terse and the gloss clarifies his argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:58.957131791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}